{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzKiqWLaFKhvajZWRDz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019xi1Ci2BHjv764Qon1nWL8","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-pzPZSo && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# ----\", s.index(\"def build_system\"))]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two blocks, two breakpoints. The static instructions come first so a change\n    # to the athlete context (a new fact, a new day) leaves that prefix cached.\n    # The second breakpoint caches the context for the rounds/messages that follow.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n'''\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache fix\n\n**Cause:** `build_system` put the instructions and the athlete context (including the\nfacts list) in one text block with a single `cache_control`. `save_fact` changes the\nfacts, so the block text changed and the whole prefix, including the ~600 static\ninstruction tokens, was re-written on the next call.\n\n**Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`):** the system prompt is now two blocks. Block 1 is\nthe static `INSTRUCTIONS` with its own breakpoint. Block 2 is `athlete_context(...)`\nwith a second breakpoint. A fact write now only invalidates block 2. Keyword tool\nfiltering is untouched, as NOTES.md asks.\n\n**Caveats (not verified, since there is no API access here):**\n- Tools come before the system prompt in the cache prefix. A message that adds a tool\n  group (plan/race) still changes the prefix and re-creates the cache. That is the\n  trade-off of the March tool filtering, and it explains some non-save_fact misses in\n  the log (e.g. the `plan_week` row).\n- The minimum cacheable prefix is about 1024 tokens for this model. Tools plus\n  instructions are estimated at 900-1000 tokens, so breakpoint 1 may fall just under\n  it. If so, the first breakpoint silently does nothing, and the fix only works once\n  that prefix is over the minimum. Check `cache_read_input_tokens` after a `save_fact`\n  in `logs/usage.jsonl`. It should stay around 900 or more instead of dropping to 0.\nE\npython3 -c \"import bot;print(bot.build_system(bot.load_athlete('42'),__import__('datetime').date.today())[1]['text'][:40])\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":25671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3d95fd4-98ec-495f-9905-7c887ddb034c","uuid":"a9a0a584-35d4-49f4-99f3-a2349a470f58","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:56:00.503Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzKibNDZnRaoPqQRULB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019xi1Ci2BHjv764Qon1nWL8":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-pzPZSo && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# ----\", s.index(\"def build_system\"))]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two blocks, two breakpoints. The static instructions come first so a change\n    # to the athlete context (a new fact, a new day) leaves that prefix cached.\n    # The second breakpoint caches the context for the rounds/messages that follow.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n'''\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache fix\n\n**Cause:** `build_system` put the instructions and the athlete context (including the\nfacts list) in one text block with a single `cache_control`. `save_fact` changes the\nfacts, so the block text changed and the whole prefix, including the ~600 static\ninstruction tokens, was re-written on the next call.\n\n**Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`):** the system prompt is now two blocks. Block 1 is\nthe static `INSTRUCTIONS` with its own breakpoint. Block 2 is `athlete_context(...)`\nwith a second breakpoint. A fact write now only invalidates block 2. Keyword tool\nfiltering is untouched, as NOTES.md asks.\n\n**Caveats (not verified, since there is no API access here):**\n- Tools come before the system prompt in the cache prefix. A message that adds a tool\n  group (plan/race) still changes the prefix and re-creates the cache. That is the\n  trade-off of the March tool filtering, and it explains some non-save_fact misses in\n  the log (e.g. the `plan_week` row).\n- The minimum cacheable prefix is about 1024 tokens for this model. Tools plus\n  instructions are estimated at 900-1000 tokens, so breakpoint 1 may fall just under\n  it. If so, the first breakpoint silently does nothing, and the fix only works once\n  that prefix is over the minimum. Check `cache_read_input_tokens` after a `save_fact`\n  in `logs/usage.jsonl`. It should stay around 900 or more instead of dropping to 0.\nE\npython3 -c \"import bot;print(bot.build_system(bot.load_athlete('42'),__import__('datetime').date.today())[1]['text'][:40])\""}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019xi1Ci2BHjv764Qon1nWL8","display_name":"Bash"}]}
